#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This example shows an option for  including suspension springs modeled in Simulink  with a single S-Function together wih a setting to avoid a timestep lag in the model.
#
#In this run, a single S-Function connects the Simulink spring forces with the VS Math Model. The kinematical preview option is used to provide information to Simulink calculated in the next timestep, avoiding lag in the calculations.
#
#Browse to the Model screen (under the button Send to Simulink) to see the checkbox to Syn exported kinematics with force imports.
#
#Browse to the Vehicle: Assembly screen and click on the suspension compliance datasets to see the settings for externally defined suspension springs.
#
#Click on the blue link "External Springs" to see how the Simulink model is connected to CarSim, and how to define the import and export variables that allow CarSim and Simulink to communicate.
#
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

